Only four studies achieved validity for lateral position, and all involved medium-fidelity simulators. These were a mix of relative and absolute validity (see Table 6 ). Alm (1996) again reported both absolute validity and no validation support on different aspects of these measures. While no significant difference was found for mean lateral position, a significant difference was found for the variation in lateral position. When the simulator motion base was off, drivers varied their position more than in the real world and with the motion base on.

